// Patch 270.  The other two .src files have had this for a long time and this
// one never did, because until public lobbies the menu had no reason to read
// JSON.  The MENU VM really does have the builtins -- pr_menu.c:2463-2472
// registers all ten in its own BuiltinList, name-resolved (#0:) exactly as
// sh_json.qc declares them -- despite that file's header comment saying SSQC
// and CSQC "both".  There is a third module and this is it.
shared/sh_json.qc
shared/sh_zonefile.qc
sui_sys.qc
shared/sh_ui.qc
// Patch 467: the feedback renderer, shared with csprogs like sui_sys.qc.
// Needs only engine builtins; m_milk.qc below is its menu owner.
milk_sys.qc

// BEFORE m_main.qc, and the dependency runs one way: m_lobby.qc holds the
// public-lobby list and knows nothing about the map picker, while m_main.qc
// draws the rows with ui_thumb and resolves each lobby's map against ms_name.
// Putting the drawing here instead would need both of those, which live below.
menu/m_lobby.qc
menu/m_pics.qc              // Patch 789: after m_lobby (Lob_NextReq), before its users
menu/m_zonedl.qc
menu/m_main.qc
// Private CSQC snapshot view; uses the picker/UI helpers and forward MF_* declarations.
menu/m_friends.qc
menu/m_chat.qc             // P963: explicit MENU lobby/DM proofs, no chat disk cache
menu/m_profile.qc          // P933: public profile preview, same read-only API as CSQC
// Patch 467: AFTER m_main.qc -- it draws with ui_option/ui_chip/ui_button and
// reads menu_screen/ms_consent, all defined there; m_main.qc reaches it
// through the MM_* prototypes beside its SCREEN_* defines.
menu/m_milk.qc
menu/m_update.qc
// ROADMAP 9: after m_main.qc for the same reason (ui_button, ui_chip, the
// create screen's state); m_main.qc and m_lobby.qc's URI_Get_Callback reach it
// through the Mlb_* prototypes.
menu/m_board.qc
// Patch 854: last, it draws with everything above (ui_*, MF_* proof, MP_Draw).
menu/m_story.qc
menu/m_home.qc             // tabbed home, after shared friends/chat/story
menu/m_mapcards.qc         // P1062: shared board transport + public identity + integer times
